hip-physical-mem-device: a fix to intel/llvm's virtual memory of the HIP adapter (hip-virtual-mem, intel/llvm's
c13ad6c7e3 on v7.2.0), applied by tools/intel_llvm_build.py.

urPhysicalMemCreate called hipMemCreate without making its device current, where the adapter's other calls
that depend on the current device do.  hipMemCreate takes the memory from the current device (ROCm 7.1.1 and
10.1: hip::getCurrentDevice()'s context), whatever device its properties name, so on a PC with two AMD GPUs a
thread whose current device was the other one would get that one's memory.  Fixed, the device is made
current first.  Read in ROCm's source; not run on two AMD GPUs.
---
diff --git a/unified-runtime/source/adapters/hip/physical_mem.cpp b/unified-runtime/source/adapters/hip/physical_mem.cpp
--- a/unified-runtime/source/adapters/hip/physical_mem.cpp
+++ b/unified-runtime/source/adapters/hip/physical_mem.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,9 @@
 // Exceptions. See https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt for license information.
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
 //
+// Modified 2026 by MistVVK and the XeStrata contributors: the device made
+// current in urPhysicalMemCreate.
+//
 //===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
 
 #include "physical_mem.hpp"
@@ -24,6 +27,9 @@
   AllocProps.location.id = hDevice->getIndex();
 
   hipMemGenericAllocationHandle_t ResHandle;
+  // hipMemCreate takes the memory from the current device, whatever device
+  // the properties name
+  ScopedDevice Active(hDevice);
   switch (auto Result = hipMemCreate(&ResHandle, size, &AllocProps, 0)) {
   case hipErrorInvalidValue:
     return UR_RESULT_ERROR_INVALID_SIZE;
